han natural gas","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://e360.yale.edu/digest/us-renewables-natural-gas-coal\"\u003ehttps://e360.yale.edu/digest/us-renewables-natural-gas-coal\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47767160\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47767160\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 147\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 142\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://e360.yale.edu/digest/us-renewables-natural-gas-coal","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47767160","date_published":"2026-04-14T15:44:15Z","author":{"name":"Brajeshwar","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=Brajeshwar"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47766550","title":"The future of everything is lies, I guess: Work","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://aphyr.com/posts/418-the-future-of-everything-is-lies-i-guess-work\"\u003ehttps://aphyr.com/posts/418-the-future-of-everything-is-lies-i-guess-work\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47766550\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47766550\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 237\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 198\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://aphyr.com/posts/418-the-future-of-everything-is-lies-i-guess-work","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47766550","date_published":"2026-04-14T15:00:45Z","author":{"name":"aphyr","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=aphyr"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47765604","title":"Rare concert recordings are landing on the Internet Archive","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/13/thousands-of-rare-concert-recordings-are-landing-on-the-internet-archive-listen-now/\"\u003ehttps://techcrunch.com/2026/04/13/thousands-of-rare-concert-recordings-are-landing-on-the-internet-archive-listen-now/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47765604\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47765604\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 486\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 145\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/13/thousands-of-rare-concert-recordings-are-landing-on-the-internet-archive-listen-now/","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47765604","date_published":"2026-04-14T13:46:31Z","author":{"name":"jrm-veris","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=jrm-veris"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47764215","title":"Ask HN: I quit my job over weaponized robots to start my own venture","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eTwo weeks ago, I quit my job at a robotics company. I was working with high-end hardware (Boston Dynamics, Unitree), but I found out they were planning to mount teleoperated weapons on the robotic platforms for a demo. I’m not willing to go there, so I resigned without another offer.\u003cp\u003eI’ve decided this is the right time to go back to entrepreneurship. We're at an incredible moment for embodied intelligence, but I feel the tools and workflows we use to interact, monitor, and control these platforms are still lagging behind.\u003cp\u003eI'm currently exploring a couple of projects around how we build, test, and interact with robots. As part of my customer discovery phase, I'm trying to gather raw data on how roboticists and developers actually work day to day and what their main pain points are regarding control interfaces.\u003cp\u003eI put together a very short survey (3 mins) to validate some ideas. If you work in robotics, embedded systems, or just tinker with hardware, your input would be incredibly valuable:\u003cp\u003eSurvey link: \u003ca href=\"https://forms.gle/3Nm76wkeT5CMt23c8\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehttps://forms.gle/3Nm76wkeT5CMt23c8\u003c/a\u003e\u003cp\u003eI'm also open to discussing the ethical lines in modern robotics or anything related to ROS2 / HRI in the thread. Thanks for reading!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47764215\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47764215\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 108\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 72\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47764215","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47764215","date_published":"2026-04-14T11:31:19Z","author":{"name":"barratia","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=barratia"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47764098","title":"NimConf 2026: Dates Announced, Registrations Open","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://nim-lang.org/blog/2026/04/07/nimconf-2026.html\"\u003ehttps://nim-lang.org/blog/2026/04/07/nimconf-2026.html\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47764098\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47764098\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 103\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 30\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://nim-lang.org/blog/2026/04/07/nimconf-2026.html","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47764098","date_published":"2026-04-14T11:19:10Z","author":{"name":"moigagoo","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=moigagoo"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47763759","title":"jj – the CLI for Jujutsu","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://steveklabnik.github.io/jujutsu-tutorial/introduction/what-is-jj-and-why-should-i-care.html\"\u003ehttps://steveklabnik.github.io/jujutsu-tutorial/introduction/what-is-jj-and-why-should-i-care.html\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47763759\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinato